==English==
{{swp}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mey- (change)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|permitten}}, borrowed from {{der|en|frm|permettre}}, from {{der|en|la|permittō||give up, allow}}, from {{m|la|per||through}} + {{m|la|mittō||send}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|most verb senses}}
*: {{IPA|en|/pɚˈmɪt/|a=GenAm}}
*: {{IPA|en|/pəˈmɪt/|a=RP}}
*: {{audio|en|en-us-permit-verb.ogg|a=US}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɪt|s=2}}
* {{sense|noun|denominal verb senses}}
*: {{IPA|en|/ˈpɝmɪt/|a=GenAm}}
*: {{IPA|en|/ˈpɜːmɪt/|a=RP}}
*: {{audio|en|en-us-permit-noun.ogg|a=US}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)mɪt|s=2}}
* {{sense|all senses}}
*: {{IPA|en|a=Indic|/ˈpər.mɪʈ/|[pɐɾ.mɪʈ]<a:rhotic>|[pɜː.mɪʈ]<a:non-rhotic>}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|++}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[allow]] (something) to [[happen]], to give [[permission]] for. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=IV|page=48|passage=Mr. Cooke at once began a tirade against the residents of Asquith for '''permitting''' a sandy and generally disgraceful condition of the roads. So roundly did he vituperate the inn management in particular, and with such a loud flow of words, that I trembled lest he should be heard on the veranda.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|title=Presbytarians|date=19 Dec 1930
|passage=Last week the decision on two points was conclusive: the Presbyterian Church in the U. S. A. will not '''permit''' ordination of women as ministers, but will '''permit''' their election as ruling elders, permission which makes possible a woman as moderator.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[allow]] (someone) to do something; to give permission to. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2009|author=Patricia Cohen|journal=New York Times|section=17 Jan 09, p. 1
|passage=He was ultimately cleared, but during that period, Mr. Ackman said, his lawyers would not '''permit''' him to defend himself publicly.}}
# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To [[grant]], or give [[permission]] for, (something) to (someone).
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=8 March 1916|title=Our Friends—Belligerents|journal=[[w:The Charlotte Observer|Charlotte Daily Observer]]|location=Charlotte, N.C.|publisher=Observer Company|page=4|pageurl=https://www.newspapers.com/newspage/616119376/|column=2|oclc=9574087|passage=The American people, more clearly than any other, have come in recent years to realize the fundamental absurdity and anachronisticity (if the word be '''permitted''' us) of war between civilized people, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[allow]] for, to make something possible. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=3 Dec 2006|author=Mary Riddell|title=Trident is a Weapon of Mass Destruction|journal=The Observer
|passage=What was left to say? Quite a lot, if only parliamentary time '''permitted'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=25 Jul 2009|author=John Mitchell|title=Clubs Preview|journal=The Guardian
|passage=For snackage there's a 1950s-themed diner plus a barbie on the terrace, weather '''permitting'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[allow]], to [[admit]] (of). {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Saki Reginald in Russia|story=Reginald in Russia|page=4|passage="You English are always so frivolous," said the Princess. "In Russia we have too many troubles to '''permit''' of our being light-hearted."}}per
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2007|author=Ian Jack|journal=The Guardian|section=22 Sep 07
|passage="As an instrument of economic policy, incantation does not '''permit''' of minor doubts or scruples."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|pronounced like noun}} To grant formal [[authorization]] for (something).
#: {{ux|en|The Building Department '''permitted''' that project last week.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Ezra Klein|title=Transcript: Ezra Klein Interviews Jesse Jenkins|date=2022-09-20|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/20/podcasts/transcript-ezra-klein-interviews-jesse-jenkins.html|quotee=Jesse Jenkins|passage={{...|And so even though transmission lines are especially bulk transmission lines are clearly related to interstate commerce and that Congress has used the Commerce Clause and the fact that the federal government should regulate interstate commerce to enact all kinds of Federal Regulations over wholesale or bulk power generation,}} they have not expanded so far federal permitting authority to site and '''permit''' transmission lines that are important for interstate commerce.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251029122741/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/20/podcasts/transcript-ezra-klein-interviews-jesse-jenkins.html|archivedate=29 October 2025}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|pronounced like noun}} To attempt to obtain or succeed in obtaining formal authorization for (something).
#: {{ux|en|We've been busy '''permitting''' the State Street development.}}
# {{lb|en|now|_|archaic|rare}} To [[hand over]], [[resign]] (something to someone). {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Addison Cato|16|passage=Let us not aggravate our sorrows, / But to the gods '''permit''' the event of things.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This is a [[catenative]] verb that in the active form takes the ''gerund (-ing)'', but in passive takes the ''to infinitive''. See [[Appendix:English catenative verbs]]

